{
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Falling Bomb",
 "category": "Effects",
 "text": "Sound: the long, whistling fall of a bomb (or a dive-bombing synth): a pitch dropping for two seconds, ending in a low boom.\n\nHow it's built: a sine whose FM gets an envelope with a 2-second DECAY at 4 octaves: the note starts four octaves up and slides all the way down. A second envelope brings in low noise through a filter at the end for the boom. A Reverb.\n\nPlay: hold a key. Higher keys fall from higher.\n\nTweak: the fall envelope's DECAY (the length of the fall), the oscillator's FM (from how high), the boom envelope's ATTACK.",
